sequenceDiagram
  participant G as Grove
  participant L as Grove shared job function
  participant R as Independently resolved Ravel
  participant H as Managed session
  Note over G,H: Lifecycle: bare grove
  G->>G: Pick leaf, compose unchanged prompt and both exact ending commands
  G->>G: Allocate launch directory, epoch admission and stdout capture
  G->>L: Public lifecycle arguments, no named parameter
  L->>R: Spawn in working-tree root as a foreground job
  R->>H: Select, then supervise with fresh ending context
  opt Finish after confirmed teardown
    H->>G: grove-llm record-teardown in this launch directory
  end
  H->>R: Exact canonical end-session grove-continue or grove-force-stop
  R-->>L: Public stdout result and status after cleanup
  L-->>G: Reaped ravel, interruption if caught, terminal restored
  G->>G: Invalidate epoch then apply interruption, successful force-stop, teardown, continuation
  Note over G,H: Standalone: grove run KIND
  G->>G: Stage private cwd, inputs and output instructions, scrub tree authority
  G->>L: start-session with --confine and explicit --runtime-read grants
  L->>R: Spawn as a detached job: own session, EOF stdin, no terminal
  R->>H: Select outside confinement, supervise inside it
  H->>H: Write declared outputs
  H->>R: Exact canonical end-session grove-continue or grove-force-stop
  R-->>L: Result and status after cleanup
  L-->>G: Reaped ravel and any caught cancellation
  alt Successful status and exact grove-continue
    G->>G: Validate and publish outputs
  else Force-stop or any other unsuccessful ending
    G->>G: Report failure, publish no outputs
  end
